        "original_id": "5e1f3a09-1f74-5843-8f2f-126779270757",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Coffee cherry tea, cascara sagrada tea\n- Plants: Rhamnus purshiana, cascara buckthorn, buckthorn\n- Places: Western North America, southern British Columbia, central California, northwestern Montana\n- Concepts: Plant-based laxatives, synonyms, common names\n\nFacts:\n- Coffee cherry tea is different from cascara sagrada tea, which is a powerful plant-based laxative.\n- Rhamnus purshiana is also known as cascara buckthorn, cascara, bearberry, chittem, and chitticum.\n- Rhamnus purshiana has the synonyms Frangula purshiana and Rhamnus purshianus.\n- Rhamnus purshiana is a species of buckthorn native to western North America.\n- Rhamnus purshiana ranges from southern British Columbia south to central California and east to northwestern Montana.",
